<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Trushko et al. (2020) Dev. Cell & Hannezo et al. (2014) PNAS Föppl-von Kármán / 3D triangulated-shell spherical epithelial cyst buckling under alginate confinement — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: section banners name the Lean law each solver implements; the per-loop math KG now registers 5 equations (Laws 1-5) each with a single `file#La-Lb` `code_locus` (secondary ranges in `code_locus_secondary`) and the Law 3 locus was corrected to the current ring/regime range; in-code comments explain the umbrella-Laplacian curvature normalisation, the sqrt(g) growth convention and the per-step imperfection re-seeding. Deductions: the ring's fitted constants (lines 205-212, 268), the 0.08 / 0.695 / 0.9985 literals and the panel-D closed form carry no derivation or citation (-6); the `seed` parameter of the ring and the `Gamma_myo` dependence of the fold-depth law are undocumented (-3); the fold-detection thresholds and contact stiffness are documented only in the dataset JSON, not at the code site (-3); measurement `method` strings for the ring still describe it as an FvK minimiser (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L174–L199: Ring pre-buckling branch: literals 0.08, 0.695, 0.9985 without derivation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L174-L199>",
        "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L266–L270: p_conf = P_c + 0.365 K_alg excess (0.55 + 0.45 Gamma_myo): fitted, uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L266-L270>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Trushko et al. (2020) Dev. Cell & Hannezo et al. (2014) PNAS Föppl-von Kármán / 3D triangulated-shell spherical epithelial cyst buckling under alginate confinement — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: `solve_confined_cyst_shell3d` is a genuine free energy minimiser (harmonic springs with rest length sqrt(g) l0, discrete Helfrich bending (kappa/2) A_v (2H - 2H0)^2 via an umbrella Laplacian with a lagged curvature normalisation, spontaneous curvature from the Hannezo formula along the radial axis, unilateral Winkler wall, cKDTree self-contact, analytic gradients, L-BFGS-B continuation in g with re-seeded 1e-3 imperfections) on a closed icosphere (Euler chi = 2 asserted); Laws 4-5 are machine checked. Deductions: the 2D ring that still produces every regime/trajectory panel is prescribed - mode hard-wired from h/R0 (line 205), depth a fitted power law (lines 207-212), L-BFGS-B result rescaled back to the target (lines 248-251) - so it is not a Föppl-von Kármán solve as v2 scored it (-10); the 3D solver gives 12 shallow folds that coincide with the 12 five-valent vertices, i.e. a mesh-templated pattern, not the single Pogorelov fold of the experiment (-6); the capsule is as soft as the sheet (k_conf ~ 1.2 Y_2D/R0) and a stiff 68 kPa capsule does not fold by g = 1.527, so the displacement-controlled confinement physics is unresolved (-4); the apical-basal axis is the radial direction and there is no cell-level apical/basal/lateral structure, lumen pressure or division topology (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L201–L212: 2D ring: fold mode hard-wired from h/R0 < 0.082 and target fold depth from fitted constants 0.818 / 0.685 / 0.575 / 0.68 / 0.22 - prescribed, not solved <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L201-L212>",
        "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L248–L251: 2D ring: optimised profile rescaled so that its peak equals target_delta, making the minimisation a smoothing step <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L248-L251>",
        "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L421–L460: build_icosphere: subdivision 3 icosahedron carries 12 five-valent vertices; the WT 12-fold pattern coincides with them (mesh-templated) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L421-L460>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Trushko et al. (2020) Dev. Cell & Hannezo et al. (2014) PNAS Föppl-von Kármán / 3D triangulated-shell spherical epithelial cyst buckling under alginate confinement — Morphometric validation: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: measurements now computed from the free 3D solver and compared with transcribed Fig. 2E data - P(t) from capsule dilation r = 0.939 (RMSE 0.089 kPa; P_3D = 0.506 kPa vs 0.485 at g = 1.527), delta(t) r = 0.799 (RMSE 0.27), Blebbistatin r = 0.813, ring-vs-shell r = 0.827 - with their Pearson p-values computed, not typed; the 12-point Zoelly scaling (r = 1.0000, slope 1.990) is an exact law check. Deductions: the ring trajectory r = 0.9927 / r = 0.998 that v2 scored is circular because the ring depth is a fitted law (-10); the free solver's headline morphometrics miss - fold depth 0.30 vs 0.64, fold count 12 vs 1, wall dilation 21 % vs a few % (-8); the H0 R0 = 0.9994 \"measurement\" is a calibration target (self-referential) (-3); p-values and stddevs of the ring and specimen measurements are hard-coded literals (1.2e-6, 2.4e-6, 4.8e-6, 1.5e-8, 2.1e-8; stddev 0.045 / 0.038 / 0.032) rather than computed (-4); the circularity reference 0.650 vs measured 0.848 is a miss not flagged in the measurement (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L1306–L1316: H0 R0 = 0.9994 vs reference 1.0: dGamma_WT was calibrated to hit this value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L1306-L1316>",
        "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L1368–L1420: Ring measurements with hard-coded p_value / stddev literals (1.0e-12, 1.2e-6, 2.4e-6, 4.8e-6; 0.045, 0.038, 0.032) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L1368-L1420>",
        "2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py L1424–L1432: Post-confluence trajectory r against Fig. 2E computed from the prescribed ring depth law - circular <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py#L1424-L1432>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-2d-fvk-ring-vs-3d-shell-wt-fold-depth-trajectory-agreement-pearson-r-over-6-g-values>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-3d-icosphere-shell-wt-e-alg-5-kpa-g-n-n-c-1-527-inward-fold-depth-delta-r0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-3d-shell-wt-capsule-pressure-p-t-k-alg-r-wall-r0-1-correlation-with-fig-2e-pressure>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-3d-shell-wt-fold-depth-trajectory-delta-t-r0-correlation-with-fig-2e-g-n-n-c-reading>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-3d-shell-wt-number-of-inward-folds-at-g-1-527-g-n-n-c-reading>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-3d-shell-wt-number-of-inward-folds-at-g-1-527-g-read-as-linear-stretch-ring-convention>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-apical-basal-spontaneous-curvature-h0-r0-of-the-wt-shell-hannezo-2014-dgamma-calibrated>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-apical-basal-tension-sweep-d-delta-r0-d-dgamma-at-g-1-52-across-5-dgamma-values>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-apical-basal-tension-sweep-d-onset-g-d-dgamma-across-5-dgamma-values>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-blebbistatin-25-um-myosin-ii-inhibited-capsule-inward-fold-depth-delta-r0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-large-thin-walled-capsule-e-alg-7-5-kpa-r0-140-um-h-r0-0-070-n-2-bilateral-fold-depth-delta-r0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-log-log-thickness-to-radius-scaling-exponent-alpha-in-pc-e-epi-h-r0-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-post-confluence-invagination-trajectory-delta-t-r0-correlation-0-to-11-h-post-confluence>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-measurement-segmented-epithelial-cyst-histology-specimen-lumen-contour-circularity>,
